<article class="env-lemma" id="016X">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/016X">Lemma <span data-tag="016X">14.8.2</span>.</a> If $U, V, W$ are simplicial objects in the category $\mathcal{C}$, and if $a : U \to V$, $b : U \to W$ are morphisms and if $V\amalg _ U W$ exists, then we have </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits (V\amalg _ U W, T) = \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits (V, T) \times _{\mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits (U, T)} \mathop{\mathrm{Mor}}\nolimits (W, T)  \]
</div>
  <p> for any fourth simplicial object $T$ of $\mathcal{C}$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
